# PocketQI's settings -- Pocket > Settings writes them in config.ini (this folder); you may also copy this file to
# config.ini and fill it in. config.ini holds your API keys: keep it private (it is never packaged nor committed).
#
# provider     the model asked first: mistral or groq (the other one is the fallback when it has a key)
# mistral_key  your Mistral API key (free: console.mistral.ai)
# groq_key     your Groq API key (free: console.groq.com)
# model        another model than the provider's default (ministral-14b-latest, qwen/qwen3.8-27b); empty: the default
# url          a server of your own: an OpenAI-compatible chat/completions address (http://192.168.1.20:8080/v1/chat/completions);
#              when set, it is the only one asked
# url_key      its key, if it wants one
# character    Pocket's character: 0 serious, 1 calm, 2 warm, 3 playful, 4 mischievous
# voice        on: Pocket speaks aloud with Mistral's voices (the Mistral key is needed); off: silent
# voice_fr     its French voice: voice_589 (Léa), fr_marie (Marie, with Pocket's moods), voice_3137 (Manon), voice_3141 (Camille)
# voice_en     its English voice: en_paul (Paul, with the moods), gb_oliver, gb_jane, voice_3150 (James)... (Pocket > Voice and Listening)
# listen       on: Pocket waits for "dis Pocket" in the background (`pocketqi --tray`, its icon in the menu bar)
# studio       on: PocketQI Studio reaches Pocket over the network (HTTPS, port 443: Pocket > PocketQI Studio...)
provider = mistral
mistral_key =
groq_key =
model =
url =
url_key =
character = 0
voice = on
voice_fr = voice_589
voice_en = en_paul
listen = off
studio = off
